 "text": "Population: Russia vs United States (1960-2026 charts)\n\n# Population in Russia compared to the United States: Trends, Charts, Rankings\n\n Updated on July 08, 2026 by Georank \n\n The latest officially reported population of Russia was 143,513,328 in 2025 vs 341,784,857 people in the United States in 2025. In 2026, based on the adjusted UN estimation, the current Russia's population is 142,643,173 people compared to 344,434,632 in the United States. \n\n## Population statistics: \n\n- The United States' population is 2.41 times bigger than Russia's. \n- Russia is ranked the 9th most populous country in the world, while the United States is the 3rd. \n- The countries together account for 5.86% of the world: 1.72% for Russia vs 4.15% for the United States. \n- For the last 10 years, Russia has had an average growth rate of -0.05% per year vs +0.65% in the United States. \n- Since 2006, the population of Russia has decreased from 143M people to 143M (0.28% decline), while the United States has grown from 298M to 344M (15.4% growth). \n\n## Russia vs United States: population by year and forecast \n\n \n\n Russia \n\n Factual \n\n Projection \n\n United States \n\n Factual \n\n Projection \n\n| Year | Population | |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| | Russia | United States |\n| 2100 | 125,631,984 | 415,429,771 |\n| 2099 | 125,735,285 | 414,829,167 |\n| 2098 | 125,835,990 | 414,231,720 |\n| 2097 | 125,914,480 | 413,576,381 |\n| 2096 | 126,004,709 | 412,927,393 |\n| 2095 | 126,072,890 | 412,225,379 |\n| 2094 | 126,125,529 | 411,498,749 |\n| 2093 | 126,181,074 | 410,785,729 |\n| 2092 | 126,256,091 | 410,051,921 |\n| 2091 | 126,304,823 | 409,320,183 |\n| 2090 | 126,360,262 | 408,613,732 |\n| 2089 | 126,412,664 | 407,885,645 |\n| 2088 | 126,463,022 | 407,129,733 |\n| 2087 | 126,511,263 | 406,421,298 |\n| 2086 | 126,579,534 | 405,715,343 |\n| 2085 | 126,655,806 | 405,059,379 |\n| 2084 | 126,730,694 | 404,343,130 |\n| 2083 | 126,805,713 | 403,612,785 |\n| 2082 | 126,889,471